ty in language between &lt;i&gt;Yishen lun&lt;/i&gt; and other manuscripts from Dunhuang and Turfan also lends support to this view.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
